      "problem": "Which of the following residue classes modulo $9$ contain the integer $-6?$\n\nI. $[2]_{9}$\n\nII. $[-3]_{9}$\n\nIII. $[3]_{9}$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $-6\\in [a]_{9}$ if \n\n$$\n-6≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-6\\notin [2]_{9}$ because $-6≢2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $-6\\notin [-3]_{9}$ because $-6≢-3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $-6\\in [3]_{9}$ because $-6≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
